window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-16cf27f48eb09b1c"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"user-lifecycle-management\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">用户生命周期管理</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需查看完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 后附加 <code>.md</code>，即可获得该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>使用本指南，可以在员工入职时授予正确的 ChatGPT 工作区访问权限，在其职责发生变化时更新访问权限，并在其离职时移除访问权限。这个流程还涵盖工作区席位、基于群组的角色、Codex 访问令牌，以及拥有自身访问控制的已连接系统。</p> <p>单点登录（SSO）用于验证员工身份。预配用于把员工添加到工作区。无论哪一项操作，单独执行时都无法决定员工的席位、功能权限、本地运行时策略或外部系统访问权限。</p> <p>应围绕三个生命周期节点管理员工访问权限：</p> <ul> <li><strong>入职：</strong> 预配工作区访问权限、群组、角色和正确的席位。</li> <li><strong>调岗：</strong> 更新员工所属的群组，并且只移除已经不再需要的直接角色。</li> <li><strong>离职：</strong> 移除工作区访问权限、撤销令牌，并检查已连接系统。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"verify-prerequisites-and-assign-owners\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">核实前提条件并指定负责人</h2> <p>在员工入职前，请确定生命周期中各个部分分别由谁负责：</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>负责人</th> <th>职责</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>工作区所有者</td> <td>启用目录同步、分配工作区角色、批准席位类型，并检查审计访问权限</td> </tr> <tr> <td>身份管理员</td> <td>配置身份提供商、应用分配、预配群组和同步状态</td> </tr> <tr> <td>工作区管理员</td> <td>检查工作区成员、群组成员关系和受支持的管理设置</td> </tr> <tr> <td>安全或服务负责人</td> <td>检查 Codex 令牌、已连接系统、共享自动化和所需审计证据</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>确认目标工作区，在需要时验证组织的电子邮件域名，并确定一位能够启用目录同步的工作区所有者。然后检查工作区套餐支持哪些控制项：</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>能力</th> <th>受支持的工作区套餐</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>通过 SCIM 进行目录同步</td> <td>ChatGPT Enterprise、Edu 和 Healthcare</td> </tr> <tr> <td>自定义角色和基于角色的访问控制</td> <td>ChatGPT Enterprise、Edu、Healthcare 和 Teachers</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Codex 访问令牌</td> <td>ChatGPT Business 和 Enterprise</td> </tr> <tr> <td>仅 Codex 席位</td> <td>符合条件的 Enterprise 工作区，以及符合资格的现有 Business 工作区；Edu、Teachers 或 Healthcare 不提供此类席位</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>SCIM 是 System for Cross-domain Identity Management（跨域身份管理系统）的缩写。Business 工作区可以支持 Codex 访问令牌而不支持 SCIM；Edu 工作区则可以支持 SCIM，但不支持 Codex 访问令牌或仅 Codex 席位。只应使用你的工作区实际提供的控制项。</p> <p>Business 工作区只有在 2026 年 6 月 24 日之前已经拥有 Codex 席位，或在该日期已有符合条件、尚待接受的 Codex 席位邀请时，才能保留和新增仅 Codex 席位。新的 Business 工作区，以及没有符合条件席位或邀请的工作区，无法添加第一个仅 Codex 席位。请参阅<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/8801890-managing-workspace-lifecycle-and-migration-in-chatgpt-business\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">在 ChatGPT Business 中管理工作区生命周期和迁移（需联网）</a>。</p> <p>如果工作区支持不止一种席位类型，请在启用自动预配前，检查 <strong>Workspace settings &gt; Identity &amp; access</strong> 中的默认值。通过 SCIM 预配的用户会继承该默认值，而席位决定其可以使用哪些产品界面。自定义角色不能授予席位本身不包含的访问权限。</p> <p>使用 <strong>Permissions &amp; roles</strong> 检查本地访问、访问令牌、凭据有效期和远程设备控制项。有些工作区会把本地访问控制合并在 <strong>Codex and Work Local</strong> 中，并提供 <strong>Allow members to use Codex and Work Locally</strong> 控制项。另一些工作区则会将 <strong>Codex Local</strong> 中的 <strong>Allow members to use Codex locally</strong> 与 <strong>Work Local</strong> 中的 <strong>Use Work locally</strong> 分开。彼此分离的 Codex 和 Work 控制项不会互相授予访问权限。令牌控制项可能显示在本地访问部分，也可能显示在单独的 <strong>Access tokens</strong> 部分。这些设置与群组成员关系和所分配的席位类型彼此独立。</p> <p>以下示例展示合并后的 <strong>Codex and Work Local</strong> 控制项，以及单独的 <strong>Access tokens</strong> 部分：</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：ChatGPT 的 Permissions &amp; roles 页面，其中显示 Codex and Work Local 访问权限、个人访问令牌和访问令牌有效期限制。</p> </blockquote> <p>有关当前前提条件和受支持的身份模式，请参阅<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/9672121\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">身份与预配（需联网）</a>以及<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/8266401-managing-members-seat-types-roles-and-access-in-chatgpt-enterprise\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">管理成员、席位类型、角色和访问权限（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-how-employees-join-the-workspace\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">选择员工加入工作区的方式</h2> <p>为每一类使用对象选择一种主要预配方式：</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>方式</th> <th>如何开始获得访问权限</th> <th>在哪里移除访问权限</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>手动邀请</td> <td>工作区所有者或管理员邀请员工</td> <td>工作区成员管理</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Automatic Account Creation</td> <td>使用符合条件电子邮件域名的员工登录</td> <td>工作区管理及相关身份流程</td> </tr> <tr> <td>通过 SCIM 进行目录同步</td> <td>身份管理员在身份提供商中分配员工</td> <td>身份提供商的应用或预配群组</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>对于未通过目录同步管理的用户，请使用手动邀请。如果工作区成员关系应随着员工入职、调岗或离职而跟随身份提供商变化，请使用 SCIM。</p> <p>不要同时启用 Automatic Account Creation 和 SCIM。通过 Automatic Account Creation 添加的用户可能不受 SCIM 管理，因此从身份提供商群组中移除这些用户，可能不会移除其工作区访问权限。有关当前指导，请参阅 <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/10011769-openai-platform-scim-integration-faq\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SCIM 集成常见问题（需联网）</a>。</p> <p>根据获批准的身份设置，SCIM 可以连接单个 ChatGPT 工作区，也可以连接组织的租户。请明确指定每个工作区和产品的分配。共享的目录连接不会自动授予或移除每个工作区或 Platform API 组织的访问权限。</p> <p><a id=\"connect-a-provisioning-group-to-the-correct-workspace\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">将预配群组连接到正确的工作区</h2> <p>请在开始预配员工之前配置连接。工作区所有者与身份管理员承担不同的职责：</p> <ol> <li>请工作区所有者选择目标 ChatGPT 工作区，并检查 <strong>Workspace settings &gt; Groups</strong>。记录现有群组名称、成员、自定义角色分配，以及相关的项目或 GPT 共享情况。</li> <li>请身份管理员确定要进行同步的准确身份提供商群组。将其名称和成员与每一个现有工作区群组进行比较。</li> <li>如果同步群组与现有工作区群组同名，请在启用同步之前协调处理或重命名冲突群组。请工作区所有者批准最终的成员、继承角色和共享情况。名称匹配的现有群组会转为由 SCIM 管理，其成员关系也会改由身份提供商控制。</li> <li>选择要预配的群组，并记录目标工作区、预期成员和群组角色分配。</li> <li>请工作区所有者打开 <strong>Workspace settings &gt; Identity &amp; access</strong>，然后选择 <strong>Enable Directory Sync</strong>。如果系统显示提示，请为工作区级预配选择 <strong>Use SCIM only for this workspace</strong>，或为获批准的租户级预配选择 <strong>Keep the option to expand across products</strong>。如果租户级 SCIM 已经启用，请管理现有连接，而不是再创建第二个工作区连接。</li> <li>请身份管理员完成身份提供商连接，选择 ChatGPT 应用，并将获批准的群组分配给该应用，以便把成员预配到目标工作区。</li> <li>在 <strong>Workspace settings &gt; Groups</strong> 中，确认所选群组显示 SCIM 徽章。在将其用于访问控制前，核实群组名称、已同步成员和目标工作区。</li> <li>请工作区所有者打开 <strong>Permissions &amp; roles &gt; Custom roles</strong>，创建或选择获批准的角色，并将其分配给同步群组。角色配置可在网页端使用，并且需要工作区所有者访问权限。</li> <li>在预配员工之前，检查群组的有效权限和工作区默认席位类型。</li> </ol> <p>身份提供商管理员控制应用和群组成员关系；工作区所有者控制目录同步和工作区角色分配。有关当前针对具体提供商的步骤和可用性，请参阅 <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/10011769-openai-platform-scim-integration-faq\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SCIM 集成常见问题（需联网）</a>和<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11750701-rbac\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">配置基于角色的访问控制（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"provision-a-new-employee\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">预配新员工</h2> <p>对于通过 SCIM 管理的员工：</p> <ol> <li>确认目标工作区、已验证的电子邮件地址、默认席位类型和身份提供商群组。</li> <li>在身份提供商中，将员工分配给 ChatGPT 应用或能够授予访问权限的群组。</li> <li>等待目录同步完成。如果员工没有出现，请检查当前身份提供商状态。</li> <li>在 <strong>Workspace settings &gt; Members</strong> 中，核实员工的电子邮件地址、成员关系或待处理邀请、席位类型和 SCIM 徽章。</li> <li>在 <strong>Workspace settings &gt; Groups</strong> 中，确认员工属于预期的同步群组。请工作区所有者核实分配给该群组的自定义角色。</li> <li>请一位具有代表性的员工登录正确的工作区，并核实其所需的具体产品界面、功能和已连接系统。</li> <li>按照组织批准的流程，记录访问权限负责人和成功核实结果。</li> </ol> <p>如果手动添加员工，请从工作区成员管理界面发送邀请，然后执行相同的席位、群组、角色和登录检查。</p> <p>群组用于组织成员，但本身不会授予每一项功能的访问权限。有关当前角色分配流程，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8\">角色与工作区权限</a>以及<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11750701-rbac\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">配置基于角色的访问控制（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"update-access-when-an-employee-changes-teams\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">员工调岗时更新访问权限</h2> <p>员工调岗后，可能仍然保留此前群组或角色分配所带来的访问权限。请先更新实际拥有成员关系的来源，再核实新的访问级别：</p> <ol> <li>确定员工的新团队、所需工作区、席位、获批准的功能权限和目标群组。</li> <li>如果员工在调岗全程必须留在工作区，请先将其添加到获批准的目标群组，再将其从原群组移除。由 SCIM 管理的成员关系应在身份提供商中更新；手动管理的成员关系应通过工作区管理界面更新。</li> <li>确认获批准的角色已经分配给目标群组。保留共享群组上现有的角色分配，让其它成员继续拥有获批准的访问权限。</li> <li>只有在单独批准群组范围的策略变更，并检查其对每位成员的影响之后，工作区所有者才能更改群组到角色的分配。</li> <li>请工作区所有者打开员工个人资料，检查 <strong>Direct roles</strong>，并移除直接分配给该员工、现已过时的角色。自定义角色使用 <strong>Default</strong>、<strong>On</strong> 和 <strong>Off</strong>。任一已分配角色中明确的 <strong>Off</strong> 都会覆盖另一个角色中的 <strong>On</strong>。</li> <li>批准团队变更前，检查员工在所有直接分配角色和群组分配角色共同作用下的有效权限。</li> <li>如果工作区支持不止一种席位类型，请工作区所有者打开 <strong>Workspace settings &gt; Members &gt; Change seat type</strong>，并检查员工预期的产品访问权限。</li> <li>将 ChatGPT 席位转换为仅 Codex 席位之前，请确认该员工应失去聊天、记忆、项目和其它 ChatGPT 功能的访问权限。底层数据不会被删除；如果员工以后恢复为 ChatGPT 席位，这些数据会再次可用。</li> <li>同步和权限更新完成后，同时核实新近允许的操作，以及那些应当不再可用的操作。</li> </ol> <p>如果员工负责某项自动化工作流，请检查其 Codex 令牌、密钥管理器条目或已连接服务授权是否应转交给另一位获批准的负责人。移除员工的本地 Codex 权限会暂停该员工的 Codex 令牌，但不会撤销这些令牌。恢复权限会让这些令牌重新生效，因此必须明确撤销那些需要永久失去访问权限的凭据。</p> <p><a id=\"remove-a-departing-employee\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">移除离职员工</h2> <p>请从实际拥有员工工作区成员关系的系统开始：</p> <ol> <li>确定该员工是由 SCIM 管理，还是由管理员手动添加。</li> <li>对于由 SCIM 管理的员工，请在身份提供商中移除该员工的 ChatGPT 应用分配，并将其从每一个能够授予访问权限的预配群组中移除。不要删除这些共享群组本身。</li> <li>对于不受 SCIM 管理的员工，请工作区所有者或管理员从 <strong>Workspace settings &gt; Members</strong> 中移除该成员。</li> <li>确认该成员已不再出现在目标工作区中。对于由 SCIM 管理的访问权限，请确认同步已经完成，而且没有其它身份提供商分配会恢复其成员关系。</li> <li>记录已完成的移除操作，并指定一位负责人检查令牌、已连接系统和保留数据。</li> </ol> <p>如果身份提供商仍然把员工分配给由 SCIM 管理的群组，请勿依赖工作区一侧的移除操作。后续同步可能会把该员工重新添加到工作区。</p> <p><a id=\"revoke-codex-access-tokens-and-transfer-automation\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"codex\">撤销 Codex 访问令牌并移交自动化</h3> <p>从工作区中移除人员，不能替代对可信自动化所用凭据的明确检查。只有当工作区支持并启用了 Codex 访问令牌时，才应使用以下流程。</p> <p>移除本地 Codex 权限会暂停现有令牌，但不会将其撤销。如果工作区所有者恢复该权限，这些令牌就可以再次工作，因此必须明确撤销那些需要永久失去访问权限的凭据。</p> <p><strong>Access tokens</strong> 页面会标明每个令牌的创建者和状态。使用 <strong>Revoke</strong> 移除有效令牌的访问权限：</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：ChatGPT 的 Access tokens 页面，其中显示令牌名称、创建者和状态，以及 Revoke 操作。</p> </blockquote> <ol> <li>请工作区所有者或管理员打开 <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/admin/access-tokens\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Access tokens（需联网）</a>。</li> <li>找出离职员工创建的令牌，以及使用这些令牌的工作流。</li> <li>选择替代身份。对于符合条件的按用量付费套餐中的持久非人工工作流，请使用获批准的专用<a href=\"#/article/a-7a5e03044e16c67c\">服务账号</a>。否则，请确定一位获批准且仍在岗的工作流负责人。必要时，请工作区所有者向该人员授予访问令牌创建权限，并确认其拥有本地 Codex 权限。</li> <li>创建替代令牌。获授权的服务账号操作人员可以从服务账号详情页创建令牌。若使用个人替代身份，请让新的工作流负责人为自己的 ChatGPT 工作区身份创建令牌。如果对话框显示 <strong>Scopes</strong>，请选择 <strong>Codex</strong>。只有工作流确有需要时才选择其它权限范围（scope）。没有 <strong>Scopes</strong> 的对话框会创建仅限 Codex 的令牌。管理员无法代表另一位用户创建个人令牌。</li> <li>更新工作流中存储的密钥，然后核实工作流能够使用替代令牌成功运行。</li> <li>请工作区所有者或管理员撤销离职员工的令牌以及所有已经被替换的凭据。</li> <li>确认已撤销的令牌无法再启动新的已验证身份运行。</li> </ol> <p>当获批准的替代负责人创建令牌时，请使用能说明用途的工作流名称，并选择组织策略允许的最短凭据有效期。如果界面显示 <strong>Scopes</strong>，请选择 <strong>Codex</strong>，并避免授予工作流不需要的权限。以下示例展示带权限范围（scope）的界面：</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：ChatGPT 的 Create access token 对话框，其中显示 Name、已选择 Codex 的 Scopes、Expiration 和 Create 操作。</p> </blockquote> <p>工作区所有者和管理员可以撤销其工作区中的任何令牌。拥有访问令牌权限的成员只能撤销自己创建的令牌。有关当前令牌权限和轮换步骤，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-f5bc151215cdfb88?anchor=rotate-or-revoke-a-token\">访问令牌</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"review-connected-systems-and-retained-data\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_8\">检查已连接系统和保留数据</h3> <p>如果该成员使用过 Work Cloud 本地计算机访问功能，请在离职检查中包含 <strong>Allow local computer access</strong> 权限和已连接的计算机。除了检查工作区和角色分配外，还要检查该成员在每个已连接系统中的访问权限。</p> <p>关闭 Work Cloud 本地计算机访问会中断正在运行的轮次。仍保有访问权限的用户可以在现有云端对话中开始新一轮；此时该对话会继续通过 Work Cloud 运行，但无法访问本地文件。这与移除工作区成员资格、撤销凭据或删除已存储数据是不同的操作。</p> <p>撤销访问权限后，分别核实以下三种结果：</p> <ul> <li><strong>正在运行的任务。</strong> 确认正在运行的任务会如何处理；对于可能仍在执行的任务，遵循已确认的 Work 事件处置与权限撤销流程。</li> <li><strong>已连接设备。</strong> 确认先前连接的设备是否仍可访问 Work。</li> <li><strong>已存储数据。</strong> 分别检查对话保留和删除情况。移除访问权限本身并不意味着已存储的数据已经删除。</li> </ul> <p>工作区预配不会管理每一处授权边界。请相关服务负责人检查以下对象的访问权限：</p> <ul> <li>源代码仓库和已连接的 GitHub 账号。</li> <li>Google Drive、Slack 及其它已连接应用。</li> <li>已安装的插件、随附 Skills 和由连接器支持的能力。</li> <li>托管 Codex 环境、共享自动化和已存储密钥。</li> <li>受管设备、本地存储的凭据和受支持的远程会话。</li> <li>单独的 Platform API 组织、项目和 API 密钥。</li> </ul> <p>请应用各系统自身负责的控制项，不要假定工作区群组或 SCIM 变更会更新所有位置的权限。有关完整的边界模型，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8\">角色与工作区权限</a>；有关插件可用性、随附 Skills 和已连接应用权限，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-20bc98306a44b420\">插件控制</a>。</p> <p>移除工作区访问权限不等于删除内容。成员离开时，工作区会自动将其项目和自定义 GPT 的所有权重新分配给工作区所有者。这些项目不会被标记为删除。如果该成员重新加入，所有权会归还给该成员。</p> <p>对于 Enterprise 和 Edu 工作区，聊天、文件和 Canvas 文档遵循所配置的工作区保留策略。Business 工作区会无限期保留聊天、文件和 Canvas 文档。Healthcare 工作区也提供数据保留控制；请检查适用的工作区配置和 <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001046-chatgpt-for-healthcare\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT for Healthcare 指南（需联网）</a>。</p> <p>重新分配项目或 GPT 不会转移原成员的私人对话或文件，工作区所有者也无法通过所有权变更查看这些私人内容。有关当前针对具体套餐的行为，请参阅<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/8266418\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">工作区成员移除和数据保留（需联网）</a>。</p> <p>如果安全或合规要求提供变更证据，请在获批准的系统中记录受影响的工作区、员工、身份提供商分配、完成时间、审批负责人和令牌撤销验证结果。在已通过身份验证的 <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/admin/api-reference\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Admin API 参考（需联网）</a>中确认可用记录、管理员权限和保留策略。敏感的合规权限范围（scope）可能要求工作区所有者权限。有关产品概览，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-9d54fab7ad7294d0\">Compliance API 和审计事件</a>。不要从本指南推断事件覆盖范围、字段或保留期限。</p> <p><a id=\"troubleshoot-missing-or-unexpected-access\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_9\">排查访问权限缺失或异常</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>现象</th> <th>要检查的内容</th> <th>纠正措施</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>员工可以登录，但找不到工作区</td> <td>目标工作区、邀请、身份提供商分配和电子邮件地址</td> <td>纠正分配或电子邮件映射，然后核实工作区成员关系</td> </tr> <tr> <td>同步的员工获得了错误的席位</td> <td>工作区默认席位类型和当前成员记录</td> <td>请工作区所有者检查默认值和该员工受支持的席位选项</td> </tr> <tr> <td>调岗后仍未移除某项功能</td> <td>其它群组成员关系、<strong>Direct roles</strong> 以及员工的组合权限</td> <td>将员工从过时群组中移除，再请工作区所有者仅撤销该员工已经过时的直接角色</td> </tr> <tr> <td>手动群组未经批准便变为由 SCIM 管理</td> <td>匹配的群组名称、身份提供商成员、继承角色和现有共享情况</td> <td>在身份提供商中协调已批准的群组成员关系，并检查受影响的访问权限</td> </tr> <tr> <td>调岗后其它员工失去访问权限</td> <td>最近对共享群组角色分配所做的更改，以及原团队获批准的访问权限</td> <td>请工作区所有者恢复获批准的共享群组角色，然后只更新调岗员工的成员关系</td> </tr> <tr> <td>调岗后自动化令牌停止工作</td> <td>工作流负责人的本地 Codex 权限和当前令牌状态</td> <td>请工作区所有者恢复获批准的本地 Codex 访问权限，或轮换并撤销受影响的令牌</td> </tr> <tr> <td>访问权限变更没有立即显示</td> <td>身份提供商同步状态、预期同步时间窗口以及近期角色更新</td> <td>请身份管理员先验证同步，再联系 OpenAI Support</td> </tr> <tr> <td>已移除的员工重新回到工作区</td> <td>身份提供商应用分配和每一个能够授予访问权限的预配群组</td> <td>在身份提供商中移除员工，而不是只在工作区设置中移除</td> </tr> <tr> <td>离职员工仍有列出的令牌</td> <td>令牌创建者、工作流负责人和工作区管理员的令牌权限</td> <td>轮换所有仍需使用的自动化凭据，然后撤销离职员工的令牌</td> </tr> <tr> <td>已连接应用仍然允许访问</td> <td>来源系统账号、插件可用性和应用授权</td> <td>请相关服务负责人使用该系统支持的控制项移除访问权限</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>大多数身份提供商每 30 至 40 分钟同步一次，但有些会立即应用更新。自定义角色变更可能需要大约五分钟才能显示。你无法强制执行 SCIM 同步，因此不要为了绕过延迟更新而移除并重新创建工作区成员。</p> <p>如果在提供商特定的预期时间窗口过后，访问权限移除或群组更新仍未完成，请让身份管理员收集以下信息：</p> <ul> <li>受影响的工作区和员工电子邮件地址。</li> <li>身份提供商、应用分配和预配群组。</li> <li>尝试执行的变更、变更时间戳和最新同步状态。</li> <li>仍需检查的直接角色、群组角色或令牌。</li> </ul> <p>请通过帮助中心联系 <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OpenAI Support（需联网）</a>，并提供这些详细信息。应将离职员工仍保留访问权限的情况视为安全例外，并遵循组织的事件升级流程。</p> <p>有关针对具体提供商的设置和同步行为，请使用当前的 <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/10011769-openai-platform-scim-integration-faq\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SCIM 集成常见问题（需联网）</a>。有关登录和身份错误，请参阅<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/10489721-login-and-authentication-faq-s-and-troubleshooting-sso-scim-and-domain-verification\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">身份验证问题排查（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"verify-the-complete-employee-lifecycle\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_10\">验证完整的员工生命周期</h2> <p>在进行更大范围的推广前，请使用一名具有代表性的测试员工验证全部三个转换过程：</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>生命周期阶段</th> <th>主要负责人</th> <th>成功结果</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>入职员工</td> <td>身份管理员</td> <td>员工以预期席位、群组和功能访问权限加入正确的工作区</td> </tr> <tr> <td>调岗员工</td> <td>身份管理员和工作区所有者</td> <td>管理员更新群组成员关系，工作区所有者移除过时的直接角色，同时保留共享群组角色</td> </tr> <tr> <td>离职员工</td> <td>身份负责人和安全负责人</td> <td>管理员移除工作区访问权限、检查受支持的令牌，并撤销或重新分配外部访问权限</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>记录每项变更由谁批准、你验证了哪些内容，以及由哪位负责人处理所有仍未解决的访问例外。请根据组织的身份和安全策略，安排定期访问权限审查。</p> <p><a id=\"related-docs\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_11\">相关文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-811aa7aeaf6b8cd4\">管理员推广指南</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-10dd8667120ae18c\">群组与预配</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8\">角色与工作区权限</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-20bc98306a44b420\">插件控制</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-f5bc151215cdfb88\">访问令牌</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7a5e03044e16c67c\">服务账号</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-1454a3aad1fa2115\">身份验证</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">托管配置</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-9d54fab7ad7294d0\">Compliance API 和审计事件</a></li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"user-lifecycle-management\">User lifecycle management</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Use this guide to give employees the right ChatGPT workspace access when they join, update that access when their responsibilities change, and remove access when they leave. The process also covers workspace seats, group-based roles, Codex access tokens, and connected systems with their own access controls.</p> <p>Single sign-on (SSO) verifies an employee's identity. Provisioning adds the employee to a workspace. Neither action alone determines the employee's seat, feature permissions, local runtime policy, or access to an external system.</p> <p>Manage employee access across three lifecycle milestones:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Join:</strong> Provision workspace access, groups, roles, and the correct seat.</li> <li><strong>Move:</strong> Update the employee's groups and remove only obsolete direct roles.</li> <li><strong>Leave:</strong> Remove workspace access, revoke tokens, and review connected systems.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"verify-prerequisites-and-assign-owners\">Verify prerequisites and assign owners</h2> <p>Before onboarding employees, identify who controls each part of the lifecycle:</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Owner</th> <th>Responsibility</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Workspace owner</td> <td>Enable directory synchronization, assign workspace roles, approve seat types, and review audit access</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Identity administrator</td> <td>Configure the identity provider, application assignments, provisioning groups, and sync status</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Workspace administrator</td> <td>Review workspace members, group membership, and supported administration settings</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Security or service owner</td> <td>Review Codex tokens, connected systems, shared automation, and required audit evidence</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Confirm the target workspace, verify the organization's email domain when required, and identify a workspace owner who can enable directory synchronization. Then check which controls the workspace plan supports:</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Capability</th> <th>Supported workspace plans</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Directory synchronization through SCIM</td> <td>ChatGPT Enterprise, Edu, and Healthcare</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Custom roles and role-based access control</td> <td>ChatGPT Enterprise, Edu, Healthcare, and Teachers</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Codex access tokens</td> <td>ChatGPT Business and Enterprise</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Codex-only seats</td> <td>Eligible Enterprise and qualifying existing Business workspaces; unavailable to Edu, Teachers, or Healthcare</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>SCIM stands for System for Cross-domain Identity Management. A Business workspace can support Codex access tokens without SCIM, while an Edu workspace can support SCIM without Codex access tokens or Codex-only seats. Apply only the controls available to your workspace.</p> <p>A Business workspace can keep and add Codex-only seats only if it had a Codex seat before June 24, 2026, or a qualifying pending Codex-seat invitation as of that date. New Business workspaces and workspaces without a qualifying seat or invitation can't add their first Codex-only seat. See <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/8801890-managing-workspace-lifecycle-and-migration-in-chatgpt-business\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Manage workspace lifecycle and migration in ChatGPT Business (online)</a>.</p> <p>Where the workspace supports more than one seat type, review the default in <strong>Workspace settings &gt; Identity &amp; access</strong> before enabling automated provisioning. SCIM-provisioned users inherit that default, and a seat controls which product surfaces are available. A custom role can't grant access that the seat doesn't include.</p> <p>Use <strong>Permissions &amp; roles</strong> to inspect local-access, access-token, credential-lifetime, and remote-device controls. Some workspaces combine local access in <strong>Codex and Work Local</strong>, with the <strong>Allow members to use Codex and Work Locally</strong> control. Others separate <strong>Codex Local</strong>, with <strong>Allow members to use Codex locally</strong>, from <strong>Work Local</strong>, with <strong>Use Work locally</strong>. Separate Codex and Work controls don't grant access to each other. Token controls appear either in the local-access section or in a separate <strong>Access tokens</strong> section. These settings are separate from group membership and assigned seat types.</p> <p>The following example shows combined <strong>Codex and Work Local</strong> controls and a separate <strong>Access tokens</strong> section:</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: ChatGPT Permissions &amp; roles showing Codex and Work Local access, personal access tokens, and the access token expiration limit.</p> </blockquote> <p>For current prerequisites and supported identity patterns, see <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/9672121\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Identity and provisioning (online)</a> and <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/8266401-managing-members-seat-types-roles-and-access-in-chatgpt-enterprise\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Manage members, seat types, roles, and access (online)</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"choose-how-employees-join-the-workspace\">Choose how employees join the workspace</h2> <p>Choose one primary provisioning method for each audience:</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Method</th> <th>How access begins</th> <th>Where to remove access</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Manual invitation</td> <td>A workspace owner or admin invites an employee</td> <td>Workspace member administration</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Automatic Account Creation</td> <td>An employee with an eligible email domain signs in</td> <td>Workspace administration and the relevant identity flow</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Directory Sync with SCIM</td> <td>An identity administrator assigns the employee in the identity provider</td> <td>The identity-provider application or provisioning group</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Use manual invitations for users who are not managed through directory synchronization. Use SCIM when workspace membership should follow the identity provider as employees join, change teams, or leave.</p> <p>Don't enable Automatic Account Creation and SCIM together. Users added through Automatic Account Creation might lack SCIM management, so removing them from an identity-provider group might not remove their workspace access. See the <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/10011769-openai-platform-scim-integration-faq\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SCIM integration FAQ (online)</a> for current guidance.</p> <p>SCIM can connect a single ChatGPT workspace or an organization's tenant, depending on the approved identity setup. Keep each workspace and product assignment explicit. A shared directory connection doesn't automatically grant or remove access across every workspace or Platform API organization.</p> <h2 id=\"connect-a-provisioning-group-to-the-correct-workspace\">Connect a provisioning group to the correct workspace</h2> <p>Configure the connection before provisioning employees. A workspace owner and an identity administrator have separate responsibilities:</p> <ol> <li>Have the workspace owner select the intended ChatGPT workspace and inspect <strong>Workspace settings &gt; Groups</strong>. Record existing group names, members, custom-role assignments, and relevant project or GPT sharing.</li> <li>Have the identity administrator identify the exact identity-provider group intended for synchronization. Compare its name and membership against every existing workspace group.</li> <li>If a synchronized group shares a name with an existing workspace group, reconcile or rename the conflicting group before enabling synchronization. Have the workspace owner approve the resulting members, inherited roles, and sharing. A matching existing group becomes SCIM-managed, and its membership switches to identity-provider control.</li> <li>Select the groups to provision and record the target workspace, expected members, and group-role assignments.</li> <li>Have the workspace owner open <strong>Workspace settings &gt; Identity &amp; access</strong> and select <strong>Enable Directory Sync</strong>. If prompted, choose <strong>Use SCIM only for this workspace</strong> for workspace-level provisioning, or <strong>Keep the option to expand across products</strong> for approved tenant-level provisioning. If tenant-level SCIM is already active, manage that existing connection instead of creating a second workspace connection.</li> <li>Have the identity administrator complete the identity-provider connection, select the ChatGPT application, and assign the approved group to provision members into the intended workspace.</li> <li>In <strong>Workspace settings &gt; Groups</strong>, confirm that the selected group displays its SCIM badge. Verify the group name, synchronized members, and target workspace before using it for access.</li> <li>Have the workspace owner open <strong>Permissions &amp; roles &gt; Custom roles</strong>, create or select the approved role, and assign it to the synchronized group. Role configuration is available on the web and requires workspace owner access.</li> <li>Review the group's effective permissions and the default workspace seat type before provisioning employees.</li> </ol> <p>The identity-provider administrator controls application and group membership; the workspace owner controls directory synchronization and workspace role assignment. See the <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/10011769-openai-platform-scim-integration-faq\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SCIM integration FAQ (online)</a> and <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11750701-rbac\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Configure role-based access control (online)</a> for current provider-specific steps and availability.</p> <h2 id=\"provision-a-new-employee\">Provision a new employee</h2> <p>For an employee managed through SCIM:</p> <ol> <li>Confirm the intended workspace, verified email address, default seat type, and identity-provider group.</li> <li>Assign the employee to the ChatGPT application or access-granting group in the identity provider.</li> <li>Allow the directory synchronization to complete. Check the current identity-provider status if the employee doesn't appear.</li> <li>In <strong>Workspace settings &gt; Members</strong>, verify the employee's email, membership or pending invitation, seat type, and SCIM badge.</li> <li>In <strong>Workspace settings &gt; Groups</strong>, confirm the employee belongs to the intended synchronized group. Have the workspace owner verify the custom role assigned to that group.</li> <li>Have a representative employee sign in to the correct workspace and verify the specific product surfaces, features, and connected systems they need.</li> <li>Record the access owner and the successful verification using your organization's approved process.</li> </ol> <p>If you add an employee manually, send the invitation from workspace member administration, then perform the same seat, group, role, and sign-in checks.</p> <p>A group organizes members but doesn't grant access to every feature by itself. For the current role-assignment procedure, see <a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8\">Roles and workspace permissions</a> and <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/11750701-rbac\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Configure role-based access control (online)</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"update-access-when-an-employee-changes-teams\">Update access when an employee changes teams</h2> <p>An employee who changes teams can keep access from previous group or role assignments. Update the source that owns the membership before verifying the new access level:</p> <ol> <li>Identify the employee's new team, required workspace, seat, approved feature permissions, and destination group.</li> <li>Add the employee to the approved destination group before removing them from their previous group if they must remain in the workspace throughout the change. Update SCIM-managed membership in the identity provider; update manually managed membership through workspace administration.</li> <li>Confirm that the approved role is already assigned to the destination group. Preserve existing role assignments on shared groups so the other members keep their approved access.</li> <li>Have a workspace owner change a group-to-role assignment only after approving a separate group-wide policy change and reviewing its effect on every member.</li> <li>Have a workspace owner open the employee's profile, review <strong>Direct roles</strong>, and remove outdated roles assigned directly to that person. Custom roles use <strong>Default</strong>, <strong>On</strong>, and <strong>Off</strong>. An explicit <strong>Off</strong> in any assigned role overrides <strong>On</strong> in another role.</li> <li>Review the employee's effective permissions across all direct and group-assigned roles before approving the team change.</li> <li>If the workspace supports more than one seat type, have a workspace owner open <strong>Workspace settings &gt; Members &gt; Change seat type</strong> and review the employee's intended product access.</li> <li>Before converting a ChatGPT seat to a Codex-only seat, confirm that the employee should lose access to chats, memories, projects, and other ChatGPT features. The underlying data isn't deleted and becomes available again if the employee returns to a ChatGPT seat.</li> <li>After synchronization and permission updates complete, verify both the newly allowed actions and the actions that should no longer be available.</li> </ol> <p>If the employee owns an automation workflow, review whether its Codex token, secret-manager entry, or connected-service authorization should move to another approved owner. Removing the employee's local Codex permission suspends that employee's Codex tokens but doesn't revoke them. Restoring the permission reactivates those tokens, so revoke credentials that must lose access permanently.</p> <h2 id=\"remove-a-departing-employee\">Remove a departing employee</h2> <p>Start with the system that owns the employee's workspace membership:</p> <ol> <li>Determine whether SCIM manages the employee or an administrator added the employee manually.</li> <li>For a SCIM-managed employee, remove that employee's ChatGPT application assignment and remove the employee from every access-granting provisioning group in the identity provider. Don't remove the shared groups themselves.</li> <li>For an employee who isn't managed through SCIM, have a workspace owner or admin remove the member from <strong>Workspace settings &gt; Members</strong>.</li> <li>Confirm that the member is no longer present in the intended workspace. For SCIM-managed access, verify that synchronization completed and that no other identity-provider assignment can restore the membership.</li> <li>Record the completed removal and assign an owner to review tokens, connected systems, and retained data.</li> </ol> <p>Don't rely on a workspace-side removal when the identity provider still assigns the employee to a SCIM-managed group. A later synchronization can add the employee back to the workspace.</p> <h3 id=\"revoke-codex-access-tokens-and-transfer-automation\">Revoke Codex access tokens and transfer automation</h3> <p>Removing a person from the workspace doesn't replace an explicit review of credentials used by trusted automation. Apply this procedure only when the workspace supports and enables Codex access tokens.</p> <p>Removing local Codex permission suspends existing tokens but doesn't revoke them. Those tokens can work again if a workspace owner restores the permission, so explicitly revoke credentials that must lose access permanently.</p> <p>The <strong>Access tokens</strong> page identifies each token's creator and status. Use <strong>Revoke</strong> to remove access from active tokens:</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: ChatGPT Access tokens showing token names, their creators and status, and the Revoke action.</p> </blockquote> <ol> <li>Have a workspace owner or admin open <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/admin/access-tokens\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Access tokens (online)</a>.</li> <li>Identify tokens created by the departing employee and the workflows using those tokens.</li> <li>Choose the replacement identity. For a durable non-human workflow on an eligible pay-as-you-go plan, use an approved dedicated <a href=\"#/article/a-7a5e03044e16c67c\">service account</a>. Otherwise, identify an approved active workflow owner. Have a workspace owner grant that person access-token creation permission if needed and confirm that the person has local Codex permission.</li> <li>Create the replacement token. A permitted service-account operator can create a token from the service account's detail page. For a personal replacement, have the new workflow owner create a token for their own ChatGPT workspace identity. If the dialog shows <strong>Scopes</strong>, select <strong>Codex</strong>. Select other scopes only when the workflow requires them. A dialog without <strong>Scopes</strong> creates a Codex-only token. An administrator can't create a personal token on another user's behalf.</li> <li>Update the workflow's stored secret, then verify that it runs successfully with the replacement token.</li> <li>Have the workspace owner or admin revoke the departing employee's tokens and any replaced credentials.</li> <li>Confirm that the revoked tokens can no longer start new authenticated runs.</li> </ol> <p>When an approved replacement owner creates a token, use a descriptive workflow name and choose the shortest credential lifetime allowed by your organization's policy. If <strong>Scopes</strong> appears, select <strong>Codex</strong> and avoid permissions the workflow doesn't require. The following example shows the scoped interface:</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: ChatGPT Create access token dialog showing Name, Scopes with Codex selected, Expiration, and the Create action.</p> </blockquote> <p>Workspace owners and admins can revoke any token in their workspace. A member with access-token permission can revoke only tokens they created. For current token permissions and rotation steps, see <a href=\"#/article/a-f5bc151215cdfb88?anchor=rotate-or-revoke-a-token\">Access tokens</a>.</p> <h3 id=\"review-connected-systems-and-retained-data\">Review connected systems and retained data</h3> <p>If the member used Local computer access with Work Cloud, include the <strong>Allow local computer access</strong> permission and connected computers in the offboarding review. Check workspace and role assignments as well as access in each connected system.</p> <p>Turning off Local computer access with Work Cloud interrupts running turns. Users who retain access can start another turn in an existing cloud conversation, which then uses Work Cloud without access to local files. This is distinct from removing workspace membership, revoking credentials, or deleting stored data.</p> <p>Review three separate outcomes after revocation:</p> <ul> <li> <p>Active tasks. Verify what happens to tasks already running and follow the confirmed Work incident and revocation procedures for any task that may still be active.</p> </li> <li> <p>Connected devices. Verify whether previously connected devices can still access Work.</p> </li> <li> <p>Stored data. Check conversation retention and deletion separately. Removing access does not by itself mean that stored data has been deleted.</p> </li> </ul> <p>Workspace provisioning doesn't manage every authorization boundary. Ask the relevant service owner to review access to:</p> <ul> <li>Source repositories and connected GitHub accounts.</li> <li>Google Drive, Slack, and other connected applications.</li> <li>Installed plugins, bundled skills, and connector-backed capabilities.</li> <li>Hosted Codex environments, shared automation, and stored secrets.</li> <li>Managed devices, locally stored credentials, and supported remote sessions.</li> <li>Separate Platform API organizations, projects, and API keys.</li> </ul> <p>Apply the controls owned by each system instead of assuming that a workspace group or SCIM change updates permissions everywhere. See <a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8\">Roles and workspace permissions</a> for the complete boundary model and <a href=\"#/article/a-20bc98306a44b420\">Plugin controls</a> for plugin availability, bundled skills, and connected-app permissions.</p> <p>Removing workspace access isn't the same as deleting content. When a member leaves, the workspace automatically reassigns their projects and custom GPT ownership to a workspace owner. Those items aren't flagged for deletion. If the member rejoins, ownership returns to that member.</p> <p>For Enterprise and Edu workspaces, chats, files, and canvas documents follow the configured workspace retention policy. Business workspaces keep chats, files, and canvas documents indefinitely. Healthcare workspaces also provide data retention controls; review the applicable workspace configuration and <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001046-chatgpt-for-healthcare\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT for Healthcare guidance (online)</a>.</p> <p>Reassigning a project or GPT doesn't transfer the former member's private conversations or files, and the workspace owner can't view that private content through the ownership change. See <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/8266418\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Workspace member removal and data retention (online)</a> for current plan-specific behavior.</p> <p>If security or compliance requires evidence of the change, record the affected workspace, employee, identity-provider assignment, completion time, approval owner, and token-revocation verification in the approved system. Confirm available records, administrator permissions, and retention in the authenticated <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/admin/api-reference\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Admin API reference (online)</a>. Sensitive compliance scopes can require a workspace owner. For the product overview, see <a href=\"#/article/a-9d54fab7ad7294d0\">Compliance API and audit events</a>. Don't infer event coverage, fields, or retention periods from this guide.</p> <h2 id=\"troubleshoot-missing-or-unexpected-access\">Troubleshoot missing or unexpected access</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Symptom</th> <th>What to check</th> <th>Corrective action</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>An employee can sign in but can't find the workspace</td> <td>The target workspace, invitation, identity-provider assignment, and email address</td> <td>Correct the assignment or email mapping, then verify workspace membership</td> </tr> <tr> <td>A synchronized employee receives the wrong seat</td> <td>The default seat type for the workspace and the current member record</td> <td>Have a workspace owner review the default and the employee's supported seat options</td> </tr> <tr> <td>A team change doesn't remove a feature</td> <td>Other group memberships, <strong>Direct roles</strong>, and the employee's combined permissions</td> <td>Remove the employee from obsolete groups, then have a workspace owner revoke only that employee's obsolete direct roles</td> </tr> <tr> <td>A manual group becomes SCIM-managed without approval</td> <td>Matching group names, identity-provider members, inherited roles, and existing sharing</td> <td>Reconcile approved group membership in the identity provider and review affected access</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Other employees lose access after a team change</td> <td>Recent changes to shared group-role assignments and the former team's approved access</td> <td>Have a workspace owner restore the approved shared group role, then update only the moving employee's membership</td> </tr> <tr> <td>An automation token stops working after a team change</td> <td>The workflow owner's local Codex permission and current token status</td> <td>Have a workspace owner restore approved local Codex access, or rotate and revoke the affected token</td> </tr> <tr> <td>An access change doesn't appear immediately</td> <td>Identity-provider sync status, the expected sync window, and recent role updates</td> <td>Have the identity administrator verify the sync before contacting OpenAI Support</td> </tr> <tr> <td>A removed employee returns to the workspace</td> <td>The identity-provider application assignment and every access-granting provisioning group</td> <td>Remove the employee in the identity provider instead of only in workspace settings</td> </tr> <tr> <td>A departing employee still has a listed token</td> <td>The token creator, workflow owner, and workspace administrator's token permissions</td> <td>Rotate any required automation credential, then revoke the departing employee's token</td> </tr> <tr> <td>A connected application still allows access</td> <td>The source system's account, plugin availability, and application grant</td> <td>Ask the relevant service owner to remove access using that system's supported controls</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Most identity providers synchronize every 30 to 40 minutes, although some apply updates immediately. Custom-role changes can take about five minutes to appear. You can't force a SCIM synchronization, so don't remove and recreate a workspace member to work around a delayed update.</p> <p>If an access removal or group update still hasn't completed after the expected provider-specific window, have the identity administrator collect:</p> <ul> <li>The affected workspace and employee email address.</li> <li>The identity provider, application assignment, and provisioning group.</li> <li>The attempted change, its timestamp, and the latest synchronization status.</li> <li>The direct roles, group roles, or tokens that still need review.</li> </ul> <p>Contact <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OpenAI Support (online)</a> with those details through the Help Center. Treat a departed employee who retains access as a security exception and follow your organization's incident-escalation process.</p> <p>For provider-specific setup and synchronization behavior, use the current <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/10011769-openai-platform-scim-integration-faq\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SCIM integration FAQ (online)</a>. For sign-in and identity errors, see <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/10489721-login-and-authentication-faq-s-and-troubleshooting-sso-scim-and-domain-verification\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Troubleshooting authentication (online)</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"verify-the-complete-employee-lifecycle\">Verify the complete employee lifecycle</h2> <p>Use a representative test employee to verify all three transitions before a broader rollout:</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Lifecycle stage</th> <th>Primary owner</th> <th>Successful outcome</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Joiner</td> <td>Identity administrator</td> <td>The employee joins the correct workspace with the intended seat, group, and feature access</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Mover</td> <td>Identity and workspace owners</td> <td>Administrators update group membership, and workspace owners remove obsolete direct roles while preserving shared group roles</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Leaver</td> <td>Identity and security owners</td> <td>Administrators remove workspace access, review supported tokens, and revoke or reassign external access</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Record who approved each change, what you verified, and which owner is responsible for resolving any remaining access exceptions. Schedule recurring access reviews according to your organization's identity and security policies.</p> <h2 id=\"related-docs\">Related docs</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-811aa7aeaf6b8cd4\">Admin rollout guide</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-10dd8667120ae18c\">Groups and provisioning</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8\">Roles and workspace permissions</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-20bc98306a44b420\">Plugin controls</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-f5bc151215cdfb88\">Access tokens</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7a5e03044e16c67c\">Service accounts</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-1454a3aad1fa2115\">Authentication</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">Managed configuration</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-9d54fab7ad7294d0\">Compliance API and audit events</a></li> </ul>"};
